  ],
  "claim": "A count-only scan of this host's Claude Code transcripts (written by Claude Code 2.1.280 to 2.1.284; scanned 2026-09-29, ccusage 20.0.26), deduplicated by message.id, covers 183,631 API calls and 1,839 advisor iterations from 2026-09-24 to 2026-09-29 (UTC dates). Its input, output, cache-read and cache-creation (5m plus 1h split) totals each match `ccusage claude daily --json --offline`, run on the same copy of the transcript tree, within 0.001%; the top-level cache_creation_input_tokens field is 2.2% higher because of tokens with no split. At Anthropic API list prices the window is $20,616 (ccusage: $19,640; the $977 difference is mostly claude-sonnet-5-5, which ccusage leaves unpriced, and the unsplit cache writes only the scan prices): children (Agent-tool and workflow stages) are 81.3% of it, workflow stages alone 66.0%, and 4 of 579 session trees cover half; in ccusage's session view the 296 workflow runs are 67.9% of its dollars (median run $22, largest $448). Cache reads are 39.5% of dollars, executor output 23.8%, cache writes 22.8%, advisor iterations 14.0%. Children with more than 60 calls are 53.4% of dollars; children of a default agent type are 63.9% of children and 41.7% of dollars; effort max covers 82.3% of calls.",
  "limitations": [
    "Local observation of one host's retained transcripts (the independent-observation class of docs/acceptance-evidence-policy.md), not a provider ledger or a bill. Both tools read one copy of the transcript tree taken at data.reconciliation.snapshot_at_utc, so their differences are method differences, not drift; a transcript that was deleted or never written is not counted, and the scan skips a line cut by the copy.",
    "The transcripts were written by more than one Claude Code release (data.scan.client_versions_by_transcript_file, 149 files without a version field); the scan and ccusage ran with the versions in data.tool_versions.",
    "Dollar figures apply Anthropic API list prices (data.prices, pricing page fetched 2026-09-29) to counted tokens. They are not what a subscription charges and do not weight the plan meter. Cache-write tokens with no 5m/1h split are priced at the 5-minute rate, and tokens of models absent from the table (data.scan.unpriced_model_tokens) are not priced. The scan-minus-ccusage difference of $977 is explained in data.reconciliation.cost_usd: claude-sonnet-5-5 ($891, unpriced by ccusage) and the unsplit cache writes ($96, which ccusage does not count), with a residual of -$10 that is not attributed.",
    "Counts only: no path, session identifier or transcript content is retained. A session tree is a main session plus every child below it, derived from the path layout; ccusage lists each workflow run as its own session, so its per-session ranking differs from data.scan.session_trees.",
    "Invocation counts are attempts, not success rates: each tool population has its own denominator (data.scan.tool_calls, mcp_calls_by_server), and a ToolSearch load is not a call. No per-tool eligible-task success rate follows from them.",
    "Cache creation: ccusage counts the 5m and 1h split (951,442,689 tokens) and the scan's split matches it; the scan also reports the top-level field (972,402,478 tokens), which exceeds the split by 20,985,862 tokens on 1,846 calls (children: 20,613,167 tokens on 1,728 calls; one main-session call reports a split larger than its top-level field and is clamped to no remainder). Which cache class the remainder belongs to is not established, and the scan prices it at the 5-minute rate. Children wrote no 1-hour-class tokens; main sessions wrote 138,475,375.",
    "Inference with no usage record is in neither the scan nor ccusage: session titles, compaction, WebFetch summaries, away summaries and the auto-mode classifier. Advisor inference is counted from usage.iterations only. Rows whose model is <synthetic> carry no usage and are skipped.",
    "Cache-miss events (data.scan.cache_misses, cache_creation_children) are calls whose cache read fell below half the previous call's context. The gap is measured between the first-written entries of consecutive calls, so it includes the next call's response time (long at effort max), and calls after a compaction also meet the rule; the 5m-1h bin is therefore approximate.",
    "The scan's rules (one row per message.id with the per-field maximum, advisor iterations, <synthetic> rows and journal files skipped, the --since filter for calls and tool counters) were checked on a synthetic fixture with hand-computed expected values and one mutant run per rule (data.control). The fixture does not check the price table or the run-shape statistics, and the reconciliation covers token totals, not dollars.",
    "The run-shape statistics describe this host and window. They do not show that fewer or shorter children lower cost at equal quality, and data.derived is arithmetic on generic price ratios; no quality comparison was run."
  ],
  "evidence_class": "independent observation: a count-only scan of this host's native Claude Code transcripts, reconciled to the upstream ccusage totals, with a synthetic-fixture check of the scan's rules and one mutant run per rule",
